{"cid": "Ugy-DdRfbJG7aJ-gu6F4AaABAg", "text": "Thanks Paul. Why don't you just use a 12V series bulb so that way you'll see real quick if there is a short, and you won't burn anything up if there is a short?? I love those little barrel power connectors. You can buy them by the 100's pretty cheap and they are easy to use. I put them in most of my battery powered testers so I don't have to use batteries. I even put one in my nice voltage standard that I have so I don't have to take it apart to install a battery when I want to use it.", "time": "7 years ago", "author": "@robertcalkjr.8325", "channel": "UCITHKFmZw337ueDJ4CB7u_Q", "votes": "0", "replies": "", "photo": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_njEQxPzyelXo5hcZOQJiRhDUdbnI__dw6rKUAojwqmgxI=s88-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj", "heart": false, "reply": false, "time_parsed": 1546032666.700488}
